<p>It only affects one person at a time. But it doesn't care about success or power specifically. It just changes the one choice they made that would've made them the happiest. For some (like Bradley) this comes out to less power. The price is, a painful death when time rolls back around. It makes the decisions of what to change, so not useful as a thaumiel, but it sticks to the deal.</p>
<p>But it also goes back in time with them, and erases itself from history and memories. The foundation found it and used it on multiple occasions, sometimes testing on D class, sometimes researchers using it. Bradley, through a combination of luck and dedication, is the first one to remember it long enough to get it back to the foundation and contained. And it was pissed at him, so made him suffer a little longer, but it doesn't have the power to escape.</p>
<p>The O5 was just a researcher when he used it, and doesn't even remember he used it. And, it continued to kill people while it was in a box and will continue to do so, because it has hopped all around time (mostly moving backwards) and those people already will have used it.</p>
